A note on dependencies

The MIT grant above covers the source code in this repository. It does not, and
cannot, relicense the third-party components a built binary links or bundles.
If you redistribute a build, those licences apply to it alongside this one.

Linked libraries:

  Qt 6            LGPL v3 (open-source edition). Widgets, Qml/Quick, Multimedia,
                  Network, Concurrent, Pdf — see native/CMakeLists.txt.
  mpv / libmpv    LGPL v2.1 or later, plus whatever its own bundled media stack
                  (FFmpeg, libass, …) carries in the build you ship.
  SDL2            zlib licence. Optional at configure time, but the released
                  desktop binaries link it — see .github/workflows/release.yml.

Vendored sources (native/third_party/, native/src/libretro/):

  Duktape 2.7.0   MIT.
  miniz 3.0.0     MIT.
  LZMA SDK        Public domain (Igor Pavlov).
  rcheevos        MIT — see native/third_party/rcheevos/LICENSE.
  libretro.h      Permissive notice from The RetroArch team, in the header
                  itself; it covers that API header only, not any core you load.

Bundled data and assets:

  Varela Round    SIL Open Font License 1.1 — see
                  native/themes2/Channels/fonts/OFL.txt.
  SDL_GameControllerDB
                  native/gamecontrollerdb.txt, under its upstream terms
                  (https://github.com/mdqinc/SDL_GameControllerDB).

Libretro cores, standalone emulators, and add-ons that the app downloads at
runtime are not part of this repository and are not covered by any of the above.
Each carries its own licence, and several are GPL.
